# DC Timer Using MOSFET PCB

A simple DC delay timer circuit that activates a buzzer after a set time delay using an RC network and a MOSFET switch.

## Overview
This project demonstrates how passive components and a MOSFET can be used to create a time-delay switching circuit suitable for alarms, reminders, or delayed activation systems.

## Key Features
- RC-based timing control
- BS107 MOSFET used as a low-side switch
- Buzzer output for audible indication
- Battery-powered operation
- Minimal component count

## How It Works
The capacitor charges through a resistor. Once the MOSFET gate voltage exceeds its threshold, the MOSFET turns on and activates the buzzer after a delay.

